                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course is designed for the age of artificial intelligence. It introduces basic methods for designing algorithms and analyzing their complexity. Topics include divide-and-conquer, greedy algorithms, dynamic programming, graph algorithms, and search techniques. The course focuses on using algorithms to model and solve real-world problems. It helps students build the ability to think clearly and solve problems on their own. Theory and practice are combined to develop algorithmic thinking and encourage creativity.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
